<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francis, Duke of Guise</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1519">1519</a>–<a href="/years/1563">1563</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as François de Lorraine, Duke of Guise</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francis, Duke of Guise, was a French general and leader of the Catholic party. He defended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metz">Metz</a> against Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> in the siege of 1552–1553 and took Calais from the English in 1558. A dominant figure at court under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a>, he opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion">French Wars of Religion</a> with the massacre of Vassy in 1562 and was assassinated by a Protestant in 1563.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francis-duke-of-guise.jpg" alt="Francis, Duke of Guise" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of François Clouet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Francis_de_Lorraine,_2nd_Duke_of_Guise_(1519%E2%80%931563),_by_Workshop_of_Fran%C3%A7ois_Clouet.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
